{"type":"message","id":"10151000","parentId":"73f38c57","timestamp":"2026-03-02T04:40:06.160Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"我看到有可用的 agent，但需要找到正确的 spawn 子命令。让我检查是否有 `agent` 命令的子命令用于 spawn subagents。","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tool-8c130f8b454d400b8ee4a93aa272ebe7","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"openclaw agent --help"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"bailian","model":"glm-5","usage":{"input":489,"output":80,"cacheRead":10077,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":10646,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1772426403298}}
{"type":"message","id":"14a65e4c","parentId":"10151000","timestamp":"2026-03-02T04:40:07.638Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"tool-8c130f8b454d400b8ee4a93aa272ebe7","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"🦞 OpenClaw 2026.2.26 (bc50708) — I keep secrets like a vault... unless you print them in debug logs again.\n\nUsage: openclaw agent [options]\n\nRun an agent turn via the Gateway (use --local for embedded)\n\nOptions:\n  --agent <id>               Agent id (overrides routing bindings)\n  --channel <channel>        Delivery channel:\n                             last|telegram|whatsapp|discord|irc|googlechat|slack|signal|imessage|feishu|nostr|msteams|mattermost|nextcloud-talk|matrix|bluebubbles|line|zalo|zalouser|synology-chat|tlon\n                             (omit to use the main session channel)\n  --deliver                  Send the agent's reply back to the selected channel\n                             (default: false)\n  -h, --help                 Display help for command\n  --json                     Output result as JSON (default: false)\n  --local                    Run the embedded agent locally (requires model\n                             provider API keys in your shell) (default: false)\n  -m, --message <text>       Message body for the agent\n  --reply-account <id>       Delivery account id override\n  --reply-channel <channel>  Delivery channel override (separate from routing)\n  --reply-to <target>        Delivery target override (separate from session\n                             routing)\n  --session-id <id>          Use an explicit session id\n  -t, --to <number>          Recipient number in E.164 used to derive the\n                             session key\n  --thinking <level>         Thinking level: off | minimal | low | medium | high\n  --timeout <seconds>        Override agent command timeout (seconds, default\n                             600 or config value)\n  --verbose <on|off>         Persist agent verbose level for the session\n\nExamples:\n  openclaw agent --to +15555550123 --message \"status update\"\n    Start a new session.\n  openclaw agent --agent ops --message \"Summarize logs\"\n    Use a specific agent.\n  openclaw agent --session-id 1234 --message \"Summarize inbox\" --thinking medium\n    Target a session with explicit thinking level.\n  openclaw agent --to +15555550123 --message \"Trace logs\" --verbose on --json\n    Enable verbose logging and JSON output.\n  openclaw agent --to +15555550123 --message \"Summon reply\" --deliver\n    Deliver reply.\n  openclaw agent --agent ops --message \"Generate report\" --deliver --reply-channel slack --reply-to \"#reports\"\n    Send reply to a different channel/target.\n\nDocs: https://docs.openclaw.ai/cli/agent"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":1472,"aggregated":"🦞 OpenClaw 2026.2.26 (bc50708) — I keep secrets like a vault... unless you print them in debug logs again.\n\nUsage: openclaw agent [options]\n\nRun an agent turn via the Gateway (use --local for embedded)\n\nOptions:\n  --agent <id>               Agent id (overrides routing bindings)\n  --channel <channel>        Delivery channel:\n                             last|telegram|whatsapp|discord|irc|googlechat|slack|signal|imessage|feishu|nostr|msteams|mattermost|nextcloud-talk|matrix|bluebubbles|line|zalo|zalouser|synology-chat|tlon\n                             (omit to use the main session channel)\n  --deliver                  Send the agent's reply back to the selected channel\n                             (default: false)\n  -h, --help                 Display help for command\n  --json                     Output result as JSON (default: false)\n  --local                    Run the embedded agent locally (requires model\n                             provider API keys in your shell) (default: false)\n  -m, --message <text>       Message body for the agent\n  --reply-account <id>       Delivery account id override\n  --reply-channel <channel>  Delivery channel override (separate from routing)\n  --reply-to <target>        Delivery target override (separate from session\n                             routing)\n  --session-id <id>          Use an explicit session id\n  -t, --to <number>          Recipient number in E.164 used to derive the\n                             session key\n  --thinking <level>         Thinking level: off | minimal | low | medium | high\n  --timeout <seconds>        Override agent command timeout (seconds, default\n                             600 or config value)\n  --verbose <on|off>         Persist agent verbose level for the session\n\nExamples:\n  openclaw agent --to +15555550123 --message \"status update\"\n    Start a new session.\n  openclaw agent --agent ops --message \"Summarize logs\"\n    Use a specific agent.\n  openclaw agent --session-id 1234 --message \"Summarize inbox\" --thinking medium\n    Target a session with explicit thinking level.\n  openclaw agent --to +15555550123 --message \"Trace logs\" --verbose on --json\n    Enable verbose logging and JSON output.\n  openclaw agent --to +15555550123 --message \"Summon reply\" --deliver\n    Deliver reply.\n  openclaw agent --agent ops --message \"Generate report\" --deliver --reply-channel slack --reply-to \"#reports\"\n    Send reply to a different channel/target.\n\nDocs: https://docs.openclaw.ai/cli/agent","cwd":"/home/one/.openclaw/agents/leader-agent/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1772426407636}}
{"type":"message","id":"cddefeb7","parentId":"14a65e4c","timestamp":"2026-03-02T04:40:12.941Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see the agents are configured, but I need to find the correct way to spawn subagents. Let me check if there's a subagent-related command. Looking at the context, I need to use `sessions_spawn` but the command I tried doesn't exist. Let me check the available commands more carefully.\n\nBased on the context provided, I should be able to spawn subagents. Let me try using the `agent` command with the specific agent name to delegate tasks.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tool-eab244a66ebe4ae286ac41fc46033298","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"openclaw subagents --help 2>/dev/null || openclaw subagent --help 2>/dev/null || echo \"checking other commands\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"bailian","model":"glm-5","usage":{"input":604,"output":234,"cacheRead":10564,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":11402,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1772426407638}}
{"type":"message","id":"641b0f94","parentId":"cddefeb7","timestamp":"2026-03-02T04:40:15.592Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"tool-eab244a66ebe4ae286ac41fc46033298","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"🦞 OpenClaw 2026.2.26 (bc50708) — I read logs so you can keep pretending you don't have to.\n\nUsage: openclaw [options] [command]\n\nOptions:\n  --dev                Dev profile: isolate state under ~/.openclaw-dev, default\n                       gateway port 19001, and shift derived ports\n                       (browser/canvas)\n  -h, --help           Display help for command\n  --log-level <level>  Global log level override for file + console\n                       (silent|fatal|error|warn|info|debug|trace)\n  --no-color           Disable ANSI colors\n  --profile <name>     Use a named profile (isolates\n                       OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR/OPENCLAW_CONFIG_PATH under\n                       ~/.openclaw-<name>)\n  -V, --version        output the version number\n\nCommands:\n  Hint: commands suffixed with * have subcommands. Run <command> --help for details.\n  acp *                Agent Control Protocol tools\n  agent                Run one agent turn via the Gateway\n  agents *             Manage isolated agents (workspaces, auth, routing)\n  approvals *          Manage exec approvals (gateway or node host)\n  browser *            Manage OpenClaw's dedicated browser (Chrome/Chromium)\n  channels *           Manage connected chat channels (Telegram, Discord, etc.)\n  clawbot *            Legacy clawbot command aliases\n  completion           Generate shell completion script\n  config *             Non-interactive config helpers (get/set/unset). Default:\n                       starts setup wizard.\n  configure            Interactive setup wizard for credentials, channels,\n                       gateway, and agent defaults\n  cron *               Manage cron jobs via the Gateway scheduler\n  daemon *             Gateway service (legacy alias)\n  dashboard            Open the Control UI with your current token\n  devices *            Device pairing + token management\n  directory *          Lookup contact and group IDs (self, peers, groups) for\n                       supported chat channels\n  dns *                DNS helpers for wide-area discovery (Tailscale + CoreDNS)\n  docs                 Search the live OpenClaw docs\n  doctor               Health checks + quick fixes for the gateway and channels\n  gateway *            Run, inspect, and query the WebSocket Gateway\n  health               Fetch health from the running gateway\n  help                 Display help for command\n  hooks *              Manage internal agent hooks\n  logs                 Tail gateway file logs via RPC\n  memory *             Search and reindex memory files\n  message *            Send, read, and manage messages\n  models *             Discover, scan, and configure models\n  node *               Run and manage the headless node host service\n  nodes *              Manage gateway-owned node pairing and node commands\n  onboard              Interactive onboarding wizard for gateway, workspace, and\n                       skills\n  pairing *            Secure DM pairing (approve inbound requests)\n  plugins *            Manage OpenClaw plugins and extensions\n  qr                   Generate iOS pairing QR/setup code\n  reset                Reset local config/state (keeps the CLI installed)\n  sandbox *            Manage sandbox containers for agent isolation\n  secrets *            Secrets runtime reload controls\n  security *           Security tools and local config audits\n  sessions *           List stored conversation sessions\n  setup                Initialize local config and agent workspace\n  skills *             List and inspect available skills\n  status               Show channel health and recent session recipients\n  system *             System events, heartbeat, and presence\n  tui                  Open a terminal UI connected to the Gateway\n  uninstall            Uninstall the gateway service + local data (CLI remains)\n  update *             Update OpenClaw and inspect update channel status\n  webhooks *           Webhook helpers and integrations\n\nExamples:\n  openclaw models --help\n    Show detailed help for the models command.\n  openclaw channels login --verbose\n    Link personal WhatsApp Web and show QR + connection logs.\n  openclaw message send --target +15555550123 --message \"Hi\" --json\n    Send via your web session and print JSON result.\n  openclaw gateway --port 18789\n    Run the WebSocket Gateway locally.\n  openclaw --dev gateway\n    Run a dev Gateway (isolated state/config) on ws://127.0.0.1:19001.\n  openclaw gateway --force\n    Kill anything bound to the default gateway port, then start it.\n  openclaw gateway ...\n    Gateway control via WebSocket.\n  openclaw agent --to +15555550123 --message \"Run summary\" --deliver\n    Talk directly to the agent using the Gateway; optionally send the WhatsApp reply.\n  openclaw message send --channel telegram --target @mychat --message \"Hi\"\n    Send via your Telegram bot.\n\nDocs: https://docs.openclaw.ai/cli"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":2643,"aggregated":"🦞 OpenClaw 2026.2.26 (bc50708) — I read logs so you can keep pretending you don't have to.\n\nUsage: openclaw [options] [command]\n\nOptions:\n  --dev                Dev profile: isolate state under ~/.openclaw-dev, default\n                       gateway port 19001, and shift derived ports\n                       (browser/canvas)\n  -h, --help           Display help for command\n  --log-level <level>  Global log level override for file + console\n                       (silent|fatal|error|warn|info|debug|trace)\n  --no-color           Disable ANSI colors\n  --profile <name>     Use a named profile (isolates\n                       OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR/OPENCLAW_CONFIG_PATH under\n                       ~/.openclaw-<name>)\n  -V, --version        output the version number\n\nCommands:\n  Hint: commands suffixed with * have subcommands. Run <command> --help for details.\n  acp *                Agent Control Protocol tools\n  agent                Run one agent turn via the Gateway\n  agents *             Manage isolated agents (workspaces, auth, routing)\n  approvals *          Manage exec approvals (gateway or node host)\n  browser *            Manage OpenClaw's dedicated browser (Chrome/Chromium)\n  channels *           Manage connected chat channels (Telegram, Discord, etc.)\n  clawbot *            Legacy clawbot command aliases\n  completion           Generate shell completion script\n  config *             Non-interactive config helpers (get/set/unset). Default:\n                       starts setup wizard.\n  configure            Interactive setup wizard for credentials, channels,\n                       gateway, and agent defaults\n  cron *               Manage cron jobs via the Gateway scheduler\n  daemon *             Gateway service (legacy alias)\n  dashboard            Open the Control UI with your current token\n  devices *            Device pairing + token management\n  directory *          Lookup contact and group IDs (self, peers, groups) for\n                       supported chat channels\n  dns *                DNS helpers for wide-area discovery (Tailscale + CoreDNS)\n  docs                 Search the live OpenClaw docs\n  doctor               Health checks + quick fixes for the gateway and channels\n  gateway *            Run, inspect, and query the WebSocket Gateway\n  health               Fetch health from the running gateway\n  help                 Display help for command\n  hooks *              Manage internal agent hooks\n  logs                 Tail gateway file logs via RPC\n  memory *             Search and reindex memory files\n  message *            Send, read, and manage messages\n  models *             Discover, scan, and configure models\n  node *               Run and manage the headless node host service\n  nodes *              Manage gateway-owned node pairing and node commands\n  onboard              Interactive onboarding wizard for gateway, workspace, and\n                       skills\n  pairing *            Secure DM pairing (approve inbound requests)\n  plugins *            Manage OpenClaw plugins and extensions\n  qr                   Generate iOS pairing QR/setup code\n  reset                Reset local config/state (keeps the CLI installed)\n  sandbox *            Manage sandbox containers for agent isolation\n  secrets *            Secrets runtime reload controls\n  security *           Security tools and local config audits\n  sessions *           List stored conversation sessions\n  setup                Initialize local config and agent workspace\n  skills *             List and inspect available skills\n  status               Show channel health and recent session recipients\n  system *             System events, heartbeat, and presence\n  tui                  Open a terminal UI connected to the Gateway\n  uninstall            Uninstall the gateway service + local data (CLI remains)\n  update *             Update OpenClaw and inspect update channel status\n  webhooks *           Webhook helpers and integrations\n\nExamples:\n  openclaw models --help\n    Show detailed help for the models command.\n  openclaw channels login --verbose\n    Link personal WhatsApp Web and show QR + connection logs.\n  openclaw message send --target +15555550123 --message \"Hi\" --json\n    Send via your web session and print JSON result.\n  openclaw gateway --port 18789\n    Run the WebSocket Gateway locally.\n  openclaw --dev gateway\n    Run a dev Gateway (isolated state/config) on ws://127.0.0.1:19001.\n  openclaw gateway --force\n    Kill anything bound to the default gateway port, then start it.\n  openclaw gateway ...\n    Gateway control via WebSocket.\n  openclaw agent --to +15555550123 --message \"Run summary\" --deliver\n    Talk directly to the agent using the Gateway; optionally send the WhatsApp reply.\n  openclaw message send --channel telegram --target @mychat --message \"Hi\"\n    Send via your Telegram bot.\n\nDocs: https://docs.openclaw.ai/cli","cwd":"/home/one/.openclaw/agents/leader-agent/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1772426415589}}
{"type":"message","id":"ed50ebb3","parentId":"641b0f94","timestamp":"2026-03-02T04:40:18.503Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see there's no `subagents` or `sessions_spawn` command available. Let me check the available skills or look at the team-tasks skill that might help with multi-agent coordination.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tool-984878f9135444f2b30029208769744e","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/one/.openclaw/skills/team-tasks/SKILL.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"bailian","model":"glm-5","usage":{"input":1055,"output":105,"cacheRead":11166,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":12326,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1772426415592}}
{"type":"message","id":"fdeb4939","parentId":"ed50ebb3","timestamp":"2026-03-02T04:40:18.511Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"tool-984878f9135444f2b30029208769744e","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nname: team-tasks\ndescription: \"多智能体开发任务协调 - 使用 JSON 任务文件协调 search/design/code/test/docs/review-agent\"\nversion: \"1.0.0\"\nmetadata:\n  openclaw:\n    requires:\n      bins: [\"python3\"]\nfiles:\n  read:\n    - <WORKSPACE>/data/team-tasks/*.json\n    - <skill>/scripts/task_manager.py\n  write:\n    - <WORKSPACE>/data/team-tasks/*.json\n---\n# Team Tasks — Multi-Agent Pipeline Coordination\n\n## Overview\n\nCoordinate dev team agents through shared JSON task files + AGI dispatch.\nAGI is the command center — agents never talk to each other directly.\n\n**Two modes:**\n- **Mode A (linear):** Fixed pipeline order `search → design → code → test → docs → review`\n- **Mode B (dag):** Tasks declare dependencies, parallel dispatch when deps are met\n\n**Available Agents:**\n- **search-agent** — Research and information gathering\n- **design-agent** — Architecture and system design\n- **code-agent** — Code implementation\n- **test-agent** — Testing and quality assurance\n- **docs-agent** — Documentation\n- **review-agent** — Code review\n\n## Task Manager CLI\n\nAll commands use: `python3 <skill-dir>/scripts/task_manager.py <command> [args]`\n\nWhere `<skill-dir>` is the directory containing this SKILL.md.\n\n### Quick Reference\n\n| Command | Mode | Usage | Description |\n|---------|------|-------|-------------|\n| `init` | both | `init <project> -g \"goal\" [-m linear\\|dag]` | Create project |\n| `add` | dag | `add <project> <task-id> -a <agent> -d <deps>` | Add task with deps |\n| `status` | both | `status <project> [--json]` | Show progress |\n| `assign` | both | `assign <project> <task> \"desc\"` | Set task description |\n| `update` | both | `update <project> <task> <status>` | Change status |\n| `next` | linear | `next <project> [--json]` | Get next stage |\n| `ready` | dag | `ready <project> [--json]` | Get all dispatchable tasks |\n| `graph` | dag | `graph <project>` | Show dependency tree |\n| `log` | both | `log <project> <task> \"msg\"` | Add log entry |\n| `result` | both | `result <project> <task> \"output\"` | Save output |\n| `reset` | both | `reset <project> [task] [--all]` | Reset to pending |\n| `list` | both | `list` | List all projects |\n\n### Status Values\n\n- `pending` — waiting for dispatch\n- `in-progress` — agent is working\n- `done` — stage completed\n- `failed` — stage failed (pipeline blocks)\n- `skipped` — intentionally skipped\n\n## Pipeline Workflow (Mode A: Linear)\n\n### Step 1: Initialize Project\n\n```bash\npython3 scripts/task_manager.py init my-project \\\n  -g \"Build a REST API with tests and docs\" \\\n  -p \"search-agent,design-agent,code-agent,test-agent,docs-agent,review-agent\"\n```\n\nDefault pipeline order: `search-agent → design-agent → code-agent → test-agent → docs-agent → review-agent`\n\n### Step 2: Assign Tasks to All Stages\n\n```bash\npython3 scripts/task_manager.py assign my-project search-agent \"Research best practices for REST API design\"\npython3 scripts/task_manager.py assign my-project design-agent \"Design API architecture: endpoints, data models, technology stack\"\npython3 scripts/task_manager.py assign my-project code-agent \"Implement REST API with Flask: GET/POST/DELETE /items\"\npython3 scripts/task_manager.py assign my-project test-agent \"Write pytest tests for all endpoints, target 90%+ coverage\"\npython3 scripts/task_manager.py assign my-project docs-agent \"Write README.md with API docs, setup guide, examples\"\npython3 scripts/task_manager.py assign my-project review-agent \"Review code quality, security, and deployment readiness\"\n```\n\n### Step 3: Dispatch Agents Sequentially\n\nFor each stage, AGI follows this loop:\n\n```\n1. Check next stage:   task_manager.py next <project> --json\n2. Mark in-progress:   task_manager.py update <project> <agent> in-progress\n3. Dispatch agent:     sessions_send(agentId=\"<agent>\", message=\"<task>\")\n4. Wait for reply      (sessions_send returns the agent's response)\n5. Save result:        task_manager.py result <project> <agent> \"<summary>\"\n6. Mark done:          task_manager.py update <project> <agent> done\n7. Repeat from 1       (currentStage auto-advances)\n```\n\n### Step 4: Handle Failures\n\nIf an agent fails:\n```bash\npython3 scripts/task_manager.py update my-project code-agent failed\npython3 scripts/task_manager.py log my-project code-agent \"Failed: syntax error in main.py\"\n```\n\nTo retry:\n```bash\npython3 scripts/task_manager.py reset my-project code-agent\npython3 scripts/task_manager.py update my-project code-agent in-progress\n# Re-dispatch...\n```\n\n### Step 5: Check Progress Anytime\n\n```bash\npython3 scripts/task_manager.py status my-project\n```\n\nOutput:\n```\n📋 Project: my-project\n🎯 Goal: Build a REST API with tests and docs\n📊 Status: active\n▶️  Current: test-agent\n\n  ✅ search-agent: done\n     Task: Research best practices for REST API design\n     Output: Found 5 relevant articles and best practices\n  🔄 design-agent: done\n     Task: Design API architecture\n     Output: Created API spec with 5 endpoints, Flask + SQLAlchemy\n  ✅ code-agent: done\n     Task: Implement REST API with Flask\n     Output: Created app.py with Flask REST API, 3 endpoints\n  🔄 test-agent: in-progress\n     Task: Write pytest tests for all endpoints\n  ⬜ docs-agent: pending\n  ⬜ review-agent: pending\n\n  Progress: [██░░] 2/6\n```\n\n## Agent Dispatch Details\n\n### Available Agents\n\n| Agent | Purpose |\n|-------|---------|\n| search-agent | Research and information gathering |\n| design-agent | Architecture and system design |\n| code-agent | Code implementation |\n| test-agent | Testing and quality assurance |\n| docs-agent | Documentation |\n| review-agent | Code review and security analysis |\n\n### Dispatch Template\n\nWhen dispatching to an agent, include:\n1. **Project context** — what the project is about\n2. **Specific task** — what this agent should do\n3. **Working directory** — where to create/find files\n4. **Previous stage output** — if relevant\n\nExample dispatch message to code-agent:\n```\nProject: my-project\nGoal: Build a REST API with tests and docs\nYour task: Implement REST API with Flask, endpoints: GET/POST/DELETE /items\nWorking directory: /home/one/projects/my-project/\nPrevious stage (design-agent) output: API spec with Flask + SQLAlchemy, 5 endpoints\n```\n\n## Mode B: DAG Workflow (Parallel Dependencies)\n\n### Step 1: Initialize DAG Project\n\n```bash\npython3 scripts/task_manager.py init my-project -m dag -g \"Build REST API with parallel workstreams\"\n```\n\n### Step 2: Add Tasks with Dependencies\n\n```bash\nTM=\"python3 scripts/task_manager.py\"\n\n# Root tasks (no deps — can run in parallel)\n$TM add my-project research   -a search-agent  --desc \"Research best practices\"\n$TM add my-project design    -a design-agent  --desc \"Design API architecture\"\n$TM add my-project scaffold  -a code-agent    --desc \"Create project skeleton\"\n\n# Tasks with dependencies\n$TM add my-project implement -a code-agent    -d \"design,scaffold\" --desc \"Implement API\"\n$TM add my-project tests    -a test-agent    -d \"design\"          --desc \"Write tests from spec\"\n$TM add my-project docs     -a docs-agent    -d \"implement\"       --desc \"Write documentation\"\n\n# Final review\n$TM add my-project review   -a review-agent  -d \"tests,docs\"      --desc \"Final code review\"\n```\n\n### Step 3: View DAG Graph\n\n```bash\n$TM graph my-project\n```\n\n### Step 4: Dispatch Ready Tasks\n\n```bash\n$TM ready my-project    # Shows all tasks whose deps are met\n```\n\nFor each ready task:\n```\n1. Get ready tasks:     task_manager.py ready <project> --json\n2. For each ready task (can dispatch in parallel):\n   a. Mark in-progress: task_manager.py update <project> <task> in-progress\n   b. Dispatch agent:   sessions_send(agentId=\"<agent>\", message=<task + context>)\n3. When agent replies:\n   a. Save result:      task_manager.py result <project> <task> \"<summary>\"\n   b. Mark done:        task_manager.py update <project> <task> done\n   c. Check newly unblocked tasks\n4. Repeat until all done\n```\n\n## Custom Pipelines\n\n### Linear (Mode A)\n```bash\n# Quick bug fix: code + test only\npython3 scripts/task_manager.py init quick-fix -g \"Hotfix\" -p \"code-agent,test-agent\"\n\n# Design first, then implement\npython3 scripts/task_manager.py init spec-driven -g \"Spec-driven dev\" -p \"search-agent,design-agent,code-agent,test-agent\"\n```\n\n### DAG (Mode B)\n```bash\n# Full pipeline with research\n$TM init full-stack -m dag -g \"Full development pipeline\"\n$TM add full-stack research  -a search-agent  --desc \"Research technologies\"\n$TM add full-stack design   -a design-agent  --desc \"Design system\"\n$TM add full-stack code     -a code-agent    --desc \"Write code\"\n$TM add full-stack test     -a test-agent    --desc \"Write tests\"\n$TM add full-stack docs     -a docs-agent    --desc \"Write docs\"\n$TM add full-stack review   -a review-agent  -d \"code,test,docs\" --desc \"Final review\"\n```\n\n## Choosing Between Modes\n\n| | Mode A (linear) | Mode B (dag) |\n|---|---|---|\n| **When** | Sequential tasks, simple flows | Parallel workstreams, complex deps |\n| **Dispatch** | One at a time, auto-advance | Multiple simultaneous, dep-driven |\n| **Setup** | `init -p agents` (one command) | `init -m dag` + `add` per task |\n| **Best for** | Bug fixes, simple features | Large features, spec-driven dev |\n\n## Data Location\n\nTask files: `~/.openclaw/data/team-tasks/<project>.json`\n\nSet custom directory:\n```bash\nexport TEAM_TASKS_DIR=/custom/path\n```\n\n## Common Pitfalls\n\n### Stage ID is agent name, NOT a number\nIn linear mode, the stage ID is the **agent name**, not a numeric index.\n\n```bash\n# ❌ WRONG\npython3 scripts/task_manager.py assign my-project 1 \"Build API\"\n\n# ✅ CORRECT\npython3 scripts/task_manager.py assign my-project code-agent \"Build API\"\npython3 scripts/task_manager.py update my-project code-agent done\npython3 scripts/task_manager.py result my-project code-agent \"Created main.py\"\n```\n\n## Tips\n\n- **One project per task** — keep scope focused\n- **Meaningful project slugs** — `rest-api-v2`, `bug-fix-auth`, `refactor-db`\n- **Save results** — always `result` before `update done`\n- **Log liberally** — helps debug failed pipelines\n- **Reset and retry** — `reset --all` for clean reruns\n- **DAG fan-out** — one root task can unblock many parallel tasks\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1772426418509}}
